For Modern English, "translation" means a complete natural-English
paraphrase of the corresponding example sentence, not a copy. Preserve the
sentence's full meaning and the sense being demonstrated, but do not use the
word or expression being defined anywhere in the paraphrase. Do not use a
capitalized, inflected, or possessive form of that term either. Reword the
sentence with an appropriate synonym or explanation while keeping it natural.
For a retained source context associated with multiple defined terms, omit
every associated term from the paraphrase.
This requirement overrides any instruction to repeat a Modern English source
sentence.
